        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#urevo-strol-2e-pro"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/410e3-vj4nL._SL500_.jpg" alt="UREVO Strol 2E Pro" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#ancheer-handle-pad"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41CghfnkBcL._SL500_.jpg" alt="ANCHEER Walking Pad with Handle Bar and 12% Incline" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#urevo-cyberpad-for-office"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/410+XTzfCUL._SL500_.jpg" alt="UREVO CyberPad for Office" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>UREVO Strol 2E Pro · ANCHEER Walking Pad with Handle Bar and 12% Incline · UREVO CyberPad for Office</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          ANCHEER treadmills turn up on Amazon at prices that make other walking pads look expensive: a pad
          with a handlebar and a 12% incline for well under $200, a "6-in-1" pad with a vibration plate for not
          much more. People searching for them usually want to know three things: whether ANCHEER still sells
          treadmills, whether they are any good, and where to find the manual for the one they already own.
          This guide answers all three, honestly, including the parts we could not confirm.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#urevo-strol-2e-pro">UREVO Strol 2E Pro</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Cheapest ANCHEER:</span> <a href="#ancheer-handle-pad">ANCHEER Walking Pad with Handle Bar and 12% Incline</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Alternative Pad:</span> <a href="#urevo-cyberpad-for-office">UREVO CyberPad for Office</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Supported Alternative:</span> <a href="#sunny-treadpad-100">Sunny Health & Fitness Treadpad 100 SF-T724064</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we tried every web address we could find for ANCHEER (ancheer.com, ancheersport.com and
          ancheer.shop): the first two would not open with a valid security certificate, and ancheer.shop sells
          only e-bikes. Amazon’s pages would not load for us that day, so we could not confirm which ANCHEER
          treadmill listings were live or what they cost. Instead we relied on independent records of ANCHEER’s
          Amazon listings: OCDevel’s walking-pad tracker (data checked 7 February 2026), PriceHistory’s tracking
          of ANCHEER listings (most recent price changes June and July 2026), Fitness Volt’s ANCHEER roundup
          (updated May 2026), third-party copies of ANCHEER manuals, and a Walmart marketplace listing; we also
          searched the US Consumer Product Safety Commission’s recall database. ANCHEER has no maker’s site to
          cross-check against, so ANCHEER figures on this page are the listing’s own claims as those sources
          recorded them; where a listing contradicts itself we say so and leave the figure off the card. The
          Sunny card uses figures and prices from Sunny's own store on 5 November 2026. On 9 November 2026 the
          ANCHEER TR6056 and UREVO SpaceWalk 3S cards, which did not come up on Amazon US, became the UREVO Strol 2E
          Pro and UREVO CyberPad, with the figures checked for our 2-in-1 folding and auto incline treadmill guides. We
          have not tested an ANCHEER machine. Prices change often, so confirm them before you order. As an
          Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">Is ANCHEER a Good Treadmill Brand? The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#what-ancheer-is">What ANCHEER Is: a Marketplace Brand</a></li>
            <li><a href="#range">The ANCHEER Treadmills on Record in 2026</a></li>
            <li><a href="#folding">ANCHEER Folding Treadmills: the Older Models</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reading-listing">How to Read an ANCHEER Listing</a></li>
            <li><a href="#manual">Finding an ANCHEER Treadmill Manual</a></li>
            <li><a href="#warranty-returns">ANCHEER Warranty, Returns and Support</a></li>
            <li><a href="#safety">Recalls and Safety</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-should-buy">Who Should Buy an ANCHEER, and the Alternatives</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Is ANCHEER a Good Treadmill Brand? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>ANCHEER walking pads can be acceptable for slow walking at a low price, but ANCHEER is a
            marketplace brand with no working treadmill website, listings that contradict themselves on motor
            and weight capacity, and support that runs entirely through Amazon.</strong> If you buy one, buy
            from a listing sold and shipped by Amazon, plan on the lowest figures in the listing, and keep it to
            walking. If you want published warranty terms and a company you can contact directly, pay a little
            more for a brand that has them.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Does ANCHEER still sell treadmills in the US?</strong> Probably, but we could not confirm it
            on the day. Independent trackers recorded several ANCHEER walking pads on Amazon through 2026: a new
            model, the TR6056, first listed in February, and price changes on other listings in June and July.
            A Walmart marketplace listing with ANCHEER as the seller carried a review from March 2026. Amazon would
            not load for us on 5 November 2026, so treat any specific listing as unconfirmed until you see it.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>What ANCHEER sells now is mostly walking pads.</strong> The full-size ANCHEER folding
            treadmills that older reviews describe appear far less often in 2026 records than its under-desk pads
            with handlebars, manual incline and, on the newest model, a <a href="/best-vibration-plates/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>vibration plate</a>. If you are looking for
            an ANCHEER folding running treadmill, you are probably looking at old stock or a used machine.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="what-ancheer-is" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What ANCHEER Is: a Marketplace Brand</h2>
<p>
            Most of the <a href="/best-treadmill-brands/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>treadmill brands</a> this site covers have a website that lists their range, publishes
            specifications and states their warranty. ANCHEER does not, at least for treadmills. On 5 November
            2026, ancheer.com and ancheersport.com would not open with a valid security certificate, and
            ancheer.shop, the one ANCHEER site that worked, sells only e-bikes. OCDevel’s tracker describes
            ANCHEER as an Amazon-only treadmill seller with no working brand site, and we found nothing to the
            contrary.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Who is behind it.</strong> The only official record we found naming a company is a 2022 CPSC
            e-bike recall, which names Shenzhen Sailvan Network Technology Ltd., doing business as ANCHEER, of
            China, as the e-bikes’ distributor. We could not confirm whether the same company sells the ANCHEER <a href="/best-treadmills-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>treadmills on Amazon</a> today. Brand names on marketplaces are sometimes licensed, sold or shared, so
            we treat the treadmill seller as unidentified beyond the name on the listing.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>What that means for you.</strong> On a marketplace listing, the brand, the seller and the
            company that ships the box can be three different parties. Your protection comes from the seller and
            from Amazon, not from a brand website. Our guide to <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">buying a treadmill on Amazon</a> explains how to tell who the seller is, and why "Ships from and sold by Amazon.com" is the line to
            look for on a brand like this.
          </p>
          <p>
            ANCHEER is not unusual in this. Many of the walking-pad brands on Amazon work the same way, and our
            guides to <a href="/maxkare-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">MaxKare</a> and <a href="/famistar-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Famistar</a> read their listings the same way this page reads ANCHEER’s.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="range" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The ANCHEER Treadmills on Record in 2026</h2>
<p>
            Because ANCHEER has no treadmill website, there is no official range to list. These are the ANCHEER
            treadmills that independent trackers, manual archives and roundups recorded on Amazon in 2026, with
            the model numbers where the listing gives one. The TR6056 did not come up when we searched Amazon US in
            November 2026, so the cards show the closest pads Amazon does list alongside ANCHEER's handlebar pad.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>TR6056 "6-in-1" walking vibration pad.</strong> First listed 4 February 2026. Walking pad with 12% manual incline, vibration plate and folding handles.</li>
            <li><strong>Walking pad with handle bar and 12% incline</strong> (ASIN B0FG28WJS2). Price-tracked between $151.99 and $179.99 from March to July 2026, against a stated $329.99.</li>
            <li><strong>12% to 15% incline walking pads</strong>, several listings tracked between about $150 and $186 in June and July 2026, including one with a vibration plate.</li>
            <li><strong>TR5972, TR5570 and TR040701 pads,</strong> whose manuals are hosted by third-party manual sites under their Amazon numbers.</li>
            <li><strong>Older folding treadmills</strong> such as the 5571B/5571ST 2-in-1 and the T900, covered in the next section.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Fitness Volt’s ANCHEER roundup, last updated in May 2026, lists six models with prices between $389.99
            and $699.99, but gives almost no specifications and says its prices are approximate. We have not
            relied on it for any figure.
          </p>
          <p>
            The first two cards below are ANCHEER pads, with only the figures their listings state consistently;
            the other two are alternatives from brands whose figures and prices we could check on their own stores
            on 5 November 2026.
          </p>
