        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does ANCHEER still sell treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Probably, on Amazon. Independent trackers recorded several ANCHEER walking pads on Amazon through 2026, including the TR6056 first listed in February 2026 and price changes on other listings in June and July. Amazon would not load for us on 5 November 2026, so we could not confirm a specific listing that day.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is ANCHEER a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              ANCHEER pads can be acceptable for slow walking at a low price, but ANCHEER has no working treadmill website, its listings contradict themselves on motor and capacity, and support runs through Amazon. Buy from a listing sold by Amazon.com and plan on the lowest published figures.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where can I find an ANCHEER treadmill manual?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check the Product guides and documents section of the Amazon listing from your order, note the model number and FCC ID from the label on the machine, then look for a copy on third-party manual archives filed under the ASIN or model number. You can also ask the seller for the manual through your Amazon order.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does an ANCHEER treadmill have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The TR6056 listing offers a one-year manufacturer warranty, but we found no published ANCHEER warranty document. In practice, the Amazon return window is your first protection, and warranty claims go through the seller via your Amazon order.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Has ANCHEER had a recall?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not for treadmills. The CPSC recalled about 22,000 ANCHEER e-bikes, model AM001907, in October 2022 because their batteries could ignite. We found no recall of any ANCHEER treadmill or walking pad when we searched on 5 November 2026.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes ANCHEER treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              ANCHEER does not say. The only official record we found is the 2022 CPSC e-bike recall, which names Shenzhen Sailvan Network Technology Ltd., doing business as ANCHEER, of China, as the distributor of the e-bikes. We could not confirm whether the same company sells the treadmills.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

